1
00:00:20,068 --> 00:00:24,678
[SPEAKER_00]: There's a question from some friends, from somewhere in the world.

2
00:00:27,744 --> 00:00:30,269
[SPEAKER_00]: The question is in regards to sexual desire.

3
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:39,945
[SPEAKER_00]: Is there anything beyond patient endurance that one should consider doing when certain thoughts arise, certain sexual thoughts arise?

4
00:00:41,126 --> 00:00:44,028
[SPEAKER_00]: For example, contemplating the different body parts and organs.

5
00:00:44,628 --> 00:00:52,613
[SPEAKER_00]: Could that not serve as a tool for trying to get rid of the unpleasant feeling of pressure and thus it would remain in the domain of

6
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,861
[SPEAKER_00]: Aversion and craving, it would be a practice done out of aversion and craving, contemplating those things.

7
00:00:59,622 --> 00:01:10,304
[SPEAKER_00]: So, is it right to do the contemplation, the super contemplation, in times when there is no unpleasant feeling or pressure, to make sure not to act out of the feeling?

8
00:01:11,485 --> 00:01:12,005
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah, yeah.

9
00:01:12,065 --> 00:01:13,085
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you should, certainly.

10
00:01:13,105 --> 00:01:14,005
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where you should do it.

11
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:20,847
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, when there is a pressure, when you are struggling to restrain yourself and so on, yeah,

12
00:01:21,819 --> 00:01:27,061
[SPEAKER_01]: Endurance there, you have to endure it, and then a subha, anything that can help you endure it.

13
00:01:27,862 --> 00:01:41,528
[SPEAKER_01]: But when there is no pressure and stuff, yeah, that's where you would actually be practicing a subha, because establishing those signs and features of a subha, when the mind is clear and mindful, oh, that will come in on its own, when the pressure of sensuality and sexuality arises.

14
00:01:42,688 --> 00:01:44,331
[SPEAKER_01]: So, so that's exactly the point.

15
00:01:44,871 --> 00:01:48,277
[SPEAKER_01]: To not wait to practice a subha only when there is a desire.

16
00:01:48,697 --> 00:01:50,700
[SPEAKER_01]: No, that's actually not going to be a proper subha.

17
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:52,904
[SPEAKER_01]: That's just going to be an absolute management of survival.

18
00:01:54,585 --> 00:01:56,987
[SPEAKER_01]: When there is no desire, that's that, yeah.

19
00:01:57,167 --> 00:02:03,452
[SPEAKER_01]: Practice the subha, dwell on it, and the clarity, the disgust of the nature of the body will be established.

20
00:02:03,592 --> 00:02:13,079
[SPEAKER_01]: And even if you don't then think about it all the time, next time sexuality presents itself, there will be the framework to the extent that you've been cultivating it when the mind was clear.

21
00:02:14,565 --> 00:02:19,288
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the more you do it, the less of that pressure will be coming your way.

22
00:02:20,029 --> 00:02:23,211
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you can reflect that you are liable to these sexual thoughts.

23
00:02:23,251 --> 00:02:23,672
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

24
00:02:23,772 --> 00:02:24,072
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

25
00:02:24,092 --> 00:02:24,953
[SPEAKER_01]: You know you are.

26
00:02:25,273 --> 00:02:27,775
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you want to... you want to... you want to practice.

27
00:02:27,795 --> 00:02:35,020
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why we say, like, you know, even the sexual desire and the pressure arises, it's a symptom of you being in a sensual domain.

28
00:02:37,275 --> 00:02:39,596
[SPEAKER_01]: But you don't want to be only dealing with that when symptoms are present.

29
00:02:39,616 --> 00:02:41,397
[SPEAKER_01]: You want to recognize, okay, now symptoms are gone.

30
00:02:41,557 --> 00:02:42,658
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm symptomless for the moment.

31
00:02:43,078 --> 00:02:44,079
[SPEAKER_01]: I have all this space to move.

32
00:02:44,359 --> 00:02:45,139
[SPEAKER_01]: Let me deal with it.

33
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,340
[SPEAKER_01]: Same for anger.

34
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:48,701
[SPEAKER_01]: Same for any unwholesome state.

35
00:02:49,281 --> 00:02:50,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Let me address it when it's not there.

36
00:02:51,062 --> 00:03:00,087
[SPEAKER_01]: Let me start contemplating what I need to contemplate, endure what I need to endure, so when it does come, I'll have something to, you know, to brace myself with.

37
00:03:01,727 --> 00:03:08,249
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's exactly... because if you... when you're doing a subha, when there is a sensual desire, you're doing it because you want to get rid of the sensual desire, because it's painful.

38
00:03:09,390 --> 00:03:18,293
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's never going to be as wholesome, as rightly ordered, as it would be if you're doing it when you have no sensual desire present.

39
00:03:18,813 --> 00:03:23,715
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you choose to contemplate a subha, and dwell on it, and maintain that theme, that clarity.

40
00:03:23,755 --> 00:03:30,077
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're neither averse, nor passionate, you're just looking at the clarity of the body, and that will settle in the deepest.

41
00:03:30,866 --> 00:03:38,451
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why when then, as I said, sensuality comes, aversion comes, well, this framework will be there, because you have been cultivating it.

42
00:03:39,232 --> 00:03:40,333
[SPEAKER_01]: It will be there on its own.

43
00:03:40,413 --> 00:03:42,434
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't need to... Where's my asubha now?

44
00:03:43,115 --> 00:03:50,180
[SPEAKER_01]: If you invested the effort before the sensuality came, asubha, the protection of that seeing the ugly, will be there.

45
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:51,942
[SPEAKER_01]: The more you develop it.

46
00:03:52,563 --> 00:03:54,286
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's not there, it means you haven't developed it sufficiently.

47
00:03:54,406 --> 00:03:55,107
[SPEAKER_01]: So, do it more.

48
00:03:55,889 --> 00:03:59,395
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you sustain the sensuality and it fades away, start doing the work.

49
00:03:59,796 --> 00:04:02,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you can't do the work and endure sensuality at the same time.

50
00:04:04,643 --> 00:04:19,326
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure, enduring centrality is a form of work, but not as efficient work as it would be when there is no centrality, and now you're going down the way of abandoning centrality when the mind is clear of it, by contemplating ugly, lack of satisfaction, that whole... all the suttas they talk about.

51
00:04:19,346 --> 00:04:20,267
[SPEAKER_01]: Vipassaness of food.

52
00:04:20,287 --> 00:04:25,428
[SPEAKER_01]: Vipassaness of food, the value of keeping the priesthood, dwelling on the unbroken virtue,

53
00:04:26,573 --> 00:04:31,095
[SPEAKER_01]: When the sensuality comes, you probably just have to endure it until it goes away.

54
00:04:31,716 --> 00:04:33,197
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you do the work.

55
00:04:33,377 --> 00:04:35,238
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you don't think, oh, I'm safe because you went away.

56
00:04:35,718 --> 00:04:36,058
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

57
00:04:36,538 --> 00:04:37,159
[SPEAKER_01]: I survived.

58
00:04:37,539 --> 00:04:39,060
[SPEAKER_01]: So, now, I need to work.

59
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:54,028
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, there's that Mahanāma in the Sutta, the noble disciple, the layperson, but he was he was in Ārya, when he asked the Buddha, how does it, like, you know, for a noble disciple, you know, dhamma is so clear, understanding, samādhi, all of that.

60
00:04:54,827 --> 00:04:59,910
[SPEAKER_01]: But, on some days, sometimes, sensuality comes and the mind just doesn't see anything.

61
00:05:00,210 --> 00:05:02,751
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter really what you recite, what's it... nothing.

62
00:05:02,911 --> 00:05:04,833
[SPEAKER_01]: All the mind sees is the sensual desire.

63
00:05:05,593 --> 00:05:17,920
[SPEAKER_01]: And the Buddha said, yeah, for as long as the... even noble disciple's mind, if he hasn't withdrawn itself sufficiently from sensuality, hasn't understood the peril of it, the gratification, that whole thing, hasn't experienced pleasure different to the pleasure of sensuality, i.e.

64
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:21,722
[SPEAKER_01]: pleasure of renunciation, the mind can still remain attracted to it on...

65
00:05:22,002 --> 00:05:28,012
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, not as much as an unrestrained, putujana, boiling mind, but still, it would go to it.

66
00:05:29,635 --> 00:05:34,643
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when it's not overwhelmed by enduring the pressure of sensuality, you do the work.

67
00:05:35,701 --> 00:05:40,003
[SPEAKER_01]: And you do a lot of it, because you have greater results of it.

68
00:05:40,243 --> 00:05:44,605
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, it's more... it will be even more efficient to do it when the mind is clear.

69
00:05:45,245 --> 00:05:50,748
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why, yes, you try and sustain your mind as clear as possible, and do the work as much as possible during that time.

70
00:05:51,248 --> 00:05:55,490
[SPEAKER_01]: Sooner or later, aversion will come, sensuality will come, sexual desire will come.

71
00:05:55,850 --> 00:05:59,312
[SPEAKER_01]: That's when you endure it, and then it goes away, back to work.

72
00:06:01,745 --> 00:06:04,207
[SPEAKER_01]: And that also can prompt you to do more work.

73
00:06:04,247 --> 00:06:06,789
[SPEAKER_01]: You realize, oh, it's still coming.

74
00:06:06,829 --> 00:06:09,531
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I'll endure it to do more work.

75
00:06:10,051 --> 00:06:10,772
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you did the work.

76
00:06:11,172 --> 00:06:11,732
[SPEAKER_01]: It's still coming.

77
00:06:12,132 --> 00:06:13,153
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not safe yet.

78
00:06:13,193 --> 00:06:13,654
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter.

79
00:06:13,894 --> 00:06:14,434
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll do the work.

80
00:06:14,574 --> 00:06:15,175
[SPEAKER_01]: It's still coming.

81
00:06:15,755 --> 00:06:16,115
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll wait.

82
00:06:16,315 --> 00:06:16,936
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, I'll do the work.

83
00:06:17,016 --> 00:06:17,556
[SPEAKER_01]: It's still coming.

84
00:06:17,636 --> 00:06:17,997
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll wait.

85
00:06:18,037 --> 00:06:18,477
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll do the work.

86
00:06:18,537 --> 00:06:19,017
[SPEAKER_01]: It's still coming.

87
00:06:19,037 --> 00:06:19,438
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll wait.

88
00:06:20,599 --> 00:06:21,639
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, it's coming less, actually.

89
00:06:21,859 --> 00:06:22,040
[SPEAKER_01]: Good.

90
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,501
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll do the work.

91
00:06:23,521 --> 00:06:25,162
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, you have confirmed that your work works.

92
00:06:26,373 --> 00:06:26,873
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, it's coming.

93
00:06:27,373 --> 00:06:28,313
[SPEAKER_01]: Slightly less, but it's coming.

94
00:06:28,393 --> 00:06:28,873
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll do the work.

95
00:06:29,354 --> 00:06:30,514
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, it's coming even less now.

96
00:06:30,754 --> 00:06:34,254
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll do even more work, because now I really know that this is working.

97
00:06:35,215 --> 00:06:36,615
[SPEAKER_01]: And now it's not coming.

98
00:06:36,655 --> 00:06:40,656
[SPEAKER_01]: Now I live in my work, which is I live in mindfulness and in renunciation.

99
00:06:41,056 --> 00:06:41,876
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's arahanty.

100
00:06:43,816 --> 00:06:47,917
[SPEAKER_01]: But when people do it in a sense of comes, I do, goes away, I succeeded.

101
00:06:48,277 --> 00:06:49,497
[SPEAKER_01]: No, that's not the work.

102
00:06:50,417 --> 00:06:53,418
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why you never overcome it, because your measure is just when it goes away.

103
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:53,918
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no.

104
00:06:54,627 --> 00:07:01,330
[SPEAKER_01]: Your measure should be how frequently it keeps coming back, how powerful it is, how much you have to endure it, and not abandon the work.

105
00:07:03,171 --> 00:07:07,973
[SPEAKER_01]: Work through that, because you are basically confirming directly for yourself that it's working.

106
00:07:08,974 --> 00:07:12,195
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not relying on a circumstance of will sensuality come or not.

107
00:07:12,356 --> 00:07:13,716
[SPEAKER_01]: If it doesn't come, maybe I'm free.

108
00:07:14,056 --> 00:07:15,217
[SPEAKER_01]: If it comes, ah...

109
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:16,340
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter.

110
00:07:16,781 --> 00:07:17,341
[SPEAKER_01]: You already...

111
00:07:17,361 --> 00:07:17,901
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm doing the work.

112
00:07:18,662 --> 00:07:20,182
[SPEAKER_01]: If it comes, it will come.

113
00:07:20,222 --> 00:07:21,123
[SPEAKER_01]: If it doesn't come, great.

114
00:07:21,523 --> 00:07:23,904
[SPEAKER_01]: When it comes, I'll just see how strong it is, how much I have to endure.

115
00:07:23,984 --> 00:07:25,645
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll endure it, because I'm accomplishing virtue.

116
00:07:26,846 --> 00:07:28,007
[SPEAKER_00]: And then I'll do the same work more.

117
00:07:28,787 --> 00:07:30,348
[SPEAKER_01]: And the time will come when it will stop coming.

118
00:07:31,168 --> 00:07:33,350
[SPEAKER_01]: And there were many similes of a similar nature that the Buddha gave.

119
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:36,171
[SPEAKER_01]: Like the flies will keep trying to come and bite and land.

120
00:07:36,591 --> 00:07:37,452
[SPEAKER_01]: If there is, you know,

121
00:07:38,743 --> 00:07:41,225
[SPEAKER_01]: Raw, whatever, dirt, present.

122
00:07:41,945 --> 00:07:44,627
[SPEAKER_01]: But if it's clean, the flies will buzz, buzz, buzz.

123
00:07:44,667 --> 00:07:46,408
[SPEAKER_01]: They'll find nothing useful to land on.

124
00:07:46,428 --> 00:07:46,888
[SPEAKER_01]: They'll leave.

125
00:07:47,609 --> 00:07:53,152
[SPEAKER_01]: Or the crows coming and trying to peck if there is fresh meat, rotten meat, stinking and something like that.

126
00:07:53,513 --> 00:07:54,853
[SPEAKER_01]: When it's gone, they'll leave.

127
00:07:54,913 --> 00:07:56,194
[SPEAKER_01]: They lose interest and they will leave.

128
00:07:56,374 --> 00:08:01,858
[SPEAKER_01]: They will be coming less and less frequently until they stop coming because of the work you're doing when they're not there.

129
00:08:02,418 --> 00:08:02,758
[SPEAKER_00]: Cleaning.

130
00:08:02,959 --> 00:08:03,419
[SPEAKER_00]: Cleaning.

131
00:08:03,619 --> 00:08:04,039
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

132
00:08:04,179 --> 00:08:05,000
[SPEAKER_01]: Polishing and cleaning.

133
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:07,241
[SPEAKER_00]: While they're not there.

134
00:08:07,341 --> 00:08:07,822
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

135
00:08:09,159 --> 00:08:12,904
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it's important to always keep that liability in your mind as a criteria.

136
00:08:12,944 --> 00:08:16,569
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like, well, most of the time I don't have sensual desire, so I'm fine.

137
00:08:18,191 --> 00:08:18,431
[SPEAKER_01]: Great.

138
00:08:18,691 --> 00:08:19,492
[SPEAKER_01]: Keep doing the work then.

139
00:08:19,512 --> 00:08:20,994
[SPEAKER_01]: Then you have no issues with doing the work.

140
00:08:21,295 --> 00:08:24,839
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the work is just a natural mode of anarahant that you're emulating through your work.

141
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:26,942
[SPEAKER_01]: Natural mode of dispassion.

142
00:08:28,123 --> 00:08:31,004
[SPEAKER_01]: But if it's like, oh, I don't need to do the work, because it doesn't come as often.

143
00:08:31,584 --> 00:08:35,565
[SPEAKER_01]: It means, you've never done any work that matters, because if you did, you would realize, can it come?

144
00:08:36,205 --> 00:08:36,886
[SPEAKER_01]: Can it still come?

145
00:08:37,406 --> 00:08:41,727
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly that, you know, the levels of purity the Buddha would still encourage monks to practice.

146
00:08:41,747 --> 00:08:50,030
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, you know, if you have mostly clean white cloth, one little stain will be visible from afar, because everything else is clean.

147
00:08:50,470 --> 00:08:51,550
[SPEAKER_01]: It will really stand out.

148
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:55,791
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, it doesn't come as often, but can it still come?

149
00:08:55,871 --> 00:08:56,071
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

150
00:08:56,872 --> 00:08:57,812
[SPEAKER_01]: That is your work now.

151
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,942
[SPEAKER_01]: You still have to work.

152
00:09:03,703 --> 00:09:06,165
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how you clean it and free yourself completely from it.

153
00:09:06,946 --> 00:09:11,029
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if it's coming frequently or not frequently, doesn't matter.

154
00:09:11,730 --> 00:09:13,591
[SPEAKER_01]: You keep doing the work when it's not there.

155
00:09:13,711 --> 00:09:15,853
[SPEAKER_01]: When it's there, you endure it and you keep reviewing your mind.

156
00:09:16,253 --> 00:09:17,014
[SPEAKER_01]: Can it still come?

157
00:09:17,334 --> 00:09:19,295
[SPEAKER_01]: Do I know that it cannot come?

158
00:09:19,736 --> 00:09:21,517
[SPEAKER_01]: Am I sure then I will not be affected?

159
00:09:22,057 --> 00:09:22,278
[SPEAKER_00]: Not.

160
00:09:22,438 --> 00:09:23,118
[SPEAKER_00]: Keep doing the work.

161
00:09:23,218 --> 00:09:24,039
[SPEAKER_00]: Keep doing the work.

162
00:09:24,059 --> 00:09:25,580
[SPEAKER_00]: What is making me liable to the

163
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:26,600
[SPEAKER_01]: What is making me liable?

164
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:31,362
[SPEAKER_01]: Keep doing the work of that restraint, accomplishment, not acting out of unwholesome, all of that.

165
00:09:31,702 --> 00:09:35,783
[SPEAKER_01]: Reviewing things, reviewing the nature of things you are attracted to, when there is no attraction.

166
00:09:36,143 --> 00:09:39,064
[SPEAKER_01]: Reviewing the nature of things you are averse to, when there is no aversion.

167
00:09:39,664 --> 00:09:44,525
[SPEAKER_01]: And cultivating and forcing your mind to deal with it, when there are no unwholesome states present.

168
00:09:44,565 --> 00:09:45,126
[SPEAKER_00]: Overwhelming.

169
00:09:45,446 --> 00:09:45,766
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

170
00:09:45,786 --> 00:09:48,507
[SPEAKER_01]: Because they will be overwhelming you and then all you would want to do is get rid of that.

171
00:09:48,587 --> 00:09:51,267
[SPEAKER_01]: So then your whole practice revolves around motivation of I don't want this pain.

172
00:09:52,208 --> 00:09:53,008
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's not a practice.

173
00:09:54,248 --> 00:10:04,070
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the work, when you're not overwhelmed by sexual thoughts, is, for example, to review the body, the organs, for example...

174
00:10:04,170 --> 00:10:06,130
[SPEAKER_01]: In a very authentic, clear manner.

175
00:10:06,290 --> 00:10:09,331
[SPEAKER_01]: Not just going anatomically without any awareness, but, no, no, no.

176
00:10:09,751 --> 00:10:19,073
[SPEAKER_01]: Things that you know you would be attracted to, that cause attraction, desire, start seeing those things when there is no desire, learning how to see them as unattractive.

177
00:10:19,876 --> 00:10:23,559
[SPEAKER_01]: Not any random thing that makes no difference to your sensuality.

178
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:40,152
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, things basically you sensually value, or things you value when you're averse, when you're not averse, or not with a mind of sensuality, that's when you go back to those things, in that mindful sense, and then learn to see them in the opposite manner.

179
00:10:40,753 --> 00:10:41,853
[SPEAKER_01]: Attractive is unattractive.

180
00:10:43,255 --> 00:10:45,316
[SPEAKER_01]: Hateful is neutral, not hateful.

181
00:10:45,376 --> 00:10:46,257
[SPEAKER_01]: Why do I need to hate this?

182
00:10:47,777 --> 00:10:54,701
[SPEAKER_01]: And sustain those themes, dwell on those themes, contemplate those themes, on the basis if you... By the way, all this can be only done on the basis of your own virtue.

183
00:10:55,141 --> 00:11:02,565
[SPEAKER_01]: If you've not been contemplating virtue, practicing virtue, keeping the virtue, all of this would just be abstract theory and response management.

184
00:11:04,106 --> 00:11:10,009
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, when it comes, you will not be too overwhelmed with, I must deal with this, because otherwise I might break.

185
00:11:10,909 --> 00:11:13,691
[SPEAKER_01]: So, hopefully, next time it will become weaker and weaker and weaker.

